fact WorkItem(id: "WI-096", description: some(value: "Proposal 025.1 Phase 1 — Proof cache (XDG, sha256, JSON). Independent of new tactic types; immediate ~6x speedup on discharge.sh. Deliverables: anthill-smt-gen/src/cache/ module (key.rs sha256 over emitted_smt_lib + canonical-serialised tactic term + ordered hint QNs + transitive rule_dep_hash + transitive fact_dep_hash + stdlib version + z3 --version + cache_format_version; store.rs JSON-per-entry with two-level hex fanout under per-solver subtree <root>/projects/<repo-hash>/proofs/z3/v1/; location.rs XDG resolver with override chain --cache-dir / ANTHILL_CACHE_DIR / anthill.toml / XDG default); anthill-cli new flags --no-cache --refresh-cache --show-cache --gc-cache --stats; wrap emit_satisfiability_check + emit_obligation call sites in anthill prove with cache lookup. Two-layer transitive dep guarantee: emitted_smt_lib bytes catch changes that surface in emission output; rule_dep_hash + fact_dep_hash catch transitive changes that don't (e.g. dep elided as dead code, or a future tactic dispatch path that consults more deps than emission). Property: for proof A whose deps are {B, C, D} where D itself depends on {D_A, D_B}, changing D_B's body or any D_B-referenced fact MUST invalidate A's cache key, at any depth — no silent stale hits possible. Risks: dep-hash correctness — DO NOT reuse requires_chain (typing.rs:1443; that walks sort-requires typeclass relations, wrong primitive). Build a fresh transitive walker over rule bodies; reuse emit_satisfiability_check_with_deps::visited_rules as the dep collection (already populated transitively during emission); for each visited rule content-hash its canonical body terms and the referenced facts' canonical fields; combine in canonical (sorted-by-QN) order. Acceptance: discharge.sh second run reports all hits and finishes <600ms wall-clock; regression test: editing a transitively-referenced fact invalidates a dependent proof's cache key. Path encoding for repo-hash with symlinks: use canonicalised paths. See docs/proposals/025.1-z3-tactic-dsl.md §Cache key + §Implementation plan Phase 1."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-04-27T16:37:17Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-096", author: "claude", content: "Phase 1 cache shipped. Module: anthill-smt-gen/src/cache/{key,store,location,mod}.rs. Cache key: sha256 over emitted_smt_lib + tactic_canon + hint_qns + transitive rule_dep_hash + transitive fact_dep_hash + stdlib + z3_version + cache_format_version. Single-walk fold: walk_visited does both content-hash + functor collection in one pass. Two-layer guarantee verified by 6 cache_key unit tests (key.rs) including the depth-2 transitive-fact change scenario. CLI wiring: dispatch_z3 looks up before solver invocation, writes verdict after; flags --no-cache / --refresh-cache / --show-cache / --gc-cache <days> / --stats / --cache-dir. End-to-end tests (anthill-cli/tests/prove_cache_test.rs, 7 tests via real CLI + real Z3 + on-disk cache): cache_hit_on_second_run, cache_invalidates_on_transitive_fact_edit (the headline correctness guarantee against the live pipeline), no_cache_flag_bypasses_lookup_and_write, refresh_cache_forces_resolver_rerun_then_writes, show_cache_lists_entries, gc_cache_removes_old_entries, stats_flag_prints_hit_miss_summary. Workspace 785 tests, 0 failures. Remaining: discharge.sh second-run-fast (<600ms) acceptance benchmark; deferred until lf1 proofs are stable.", at: "2026-04-27T16:37:18Z")
